"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[4454],{29002:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"mutate","desc":"Applies a mutator to the player\'s live `stats` table and replicates whatever\\nit reports as changed.\\n\\nThe mutator receives `profileData.stats` and returns a map of\\n`currencyType -> value`; only the keys of that map matter here \u2014 they are\\nturned into `stats.<currencyType>` paths and passed to\\n[ProfileService.update]. The mutator runs inside a pcall so a throw warns\\nand aborts rather than leaving a partially applied write unreplicated.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"balance owner","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"mutator","desc":"receives `stats`, returns changed currencies","lua_type":"(ProfileTypes.ProfileData) -> { [string]: number }"}],"returns":[{"desc":"false when the profile is unloaded or the mutator threw","lua_type":"boolean?"},{"desc":"the mutator\'s returned table, passed straight back","lua_type":"{ [string]: number }?"}],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":80,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/CurrencyService.luau"}},{"name":"init","desc":"Registers the `coins` developer-product receipt callback with\\n[MarketplaceData].\\n\\nOn a successful purchase the product\'s `value` is run through\\n`adjustValueByUserPriceLevel` for the buying player before being credited,\\nso players in different regional price tiers receive an amount matched to\\nwhat they actually paid. The callback\'s return value is the credit\'s success\\nflag, which [MarketplaceService] uses to decide whether to grant the receipt.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":123,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/CurrencyService.luau"}},{"name":"fetchStats","desc":"Returns the player\'s whole `stats` table. Falls back to a fresh\\n[DataTemplate]\'s stats when no profile is loaded, so callers always get a\\nusable table of zeroed balances rather than nil.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"balance owner","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"ProfileTypes.Stats"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":152,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/CurrencyService.luau"}},{"name":"fetchStat","desc":"Returns a single balance. Reads through [CurrencyService.fetchStats], so an\\nunloaded profile yields the template default rather than erroring.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"balance owner","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"currencyType","desc":"key under `stats`, e.g. \\"coins\\"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"number"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":169,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/CurrencyService.luau"}},{"name":"set","desc":"Overwrites a balance outright. Rejects negative amounts.\\n\\nPrefer [CurrencyService.add] / [CurrencyService.take] for gameplay flows \u2014\\n`set` discards whatever the balance was, so two concurrent grants can clobber\\neach other.\\n\\nNote that setting a balance to exactly 0 returns false: the success check\\ntreats the resulting `0` as absent.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"balance owner","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"currencyType","desc":"key under `stats`","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"amount","desc":"new balance, must be >= 0","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"whether the write applied","lua_type":"boolean?"},{"desc":"the new balance","lua_type":"number?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":194,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/CurrencyService.luau"}},{"name":"add","desc":"Credits a balance. The amount is floored, and must be strictly positive \u2014\\nuse [CurrencyService.take] to remove currency rather than adding a negative.\\n\\nReads the current balance inside the mutator, so it is safe against the\\nbalance having moved since the caller last read it.\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal ok, newBalance = CurrencyService.add(player, \\"coins\\", 250)\\n```","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"balance owner","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"currencyType","desc":"key under `stats`","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"amount","desc":"amount to credit, must be > 0","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[{"desc":"whether the write applied","lua_type":"boolean?"},{"desc":"the resulting balance","lua_type":"number?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":241,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/CurrencyService.luau"}},{"name":"take","desc":"Safe debit that will not allow the currency to go below 0 unless overridden.\\n\\nThe amount is floored and must be strictly positive. The balance is checked\\nbefore the mutation: when the player cannot afford it and `override` is not\\nset, nothing is written and the call returns `false` alongside the player\'s\\n*current* balance so the caller can report the shortfall. Passing `override`\\nskips the affordability check and permits a negative balance.\\n\\n```lua\\nlocal ok, balance = CurrencyService.take(player, \\"coins\\", price)\\nif not ok then\\n\\t-- `balance` is what they actually have\\nend\\n```","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"balance owner","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"currencyType","desc":"key under `stats`","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"amount","desc":"amount to debit, must be > 0","lua_type":"number"},{"name":"override","desc":"allow the balance to go negative","lua_type":"boolean?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"whether the debit applied","lua_type":"boolean?"},{"desc":"resulting balance on success, current balance on insufficient funds","lua_type":"number?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":293,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/CurrencyService.luau"}},{"name":"setMultiple","desc":"Overwrites several balances in a single replicated mutation. Every amount\\nmust be >= 0 or the whole call is rejected before anything is written.\\n\\n:::caution Returns the request, not the result\\nUnlike [CurrencyService.set], the second return value is the `updates` table\\nyou passed in, not the resulting balances \u2014 for a `set` these coincide.\\nNote also that the `math.floor` in the validation loop assigns to the loop\\nvariable and is discarded, so unlike the singular variants these amounts are\\nstored unfloored.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"balance owner","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"updates","desc":"currencyType -> new balance","lua_type":"{ [string]: number }"}],"returns":[{"desc":"whether the write applied","lua_type":"boolean?"},{"desc":"the `updates` table passed in","lua_type":"{ [string]: number }?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":351,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/CurrencyService.luau"}},{"name":"addMultiple","desc":"Credits several balances in a single replicated mutation. Every amount must\\nbe > 0 or the whole call is rejected before anything is written.\\n\\n:::caution Returns the deltas, not the balances\\nThe second return value is the `updates` table you passed in \u2014 the amounts\\n*added*, not the resulting balances. Read them back with\\n[CurrencyService.fetchStats] if you need the totals. The `math.floor` in the\\nvalidation loop is discarded, so amounts are stored unfloored.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"balance owner","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"updates","desc":"currencyType -> amount to credit","lua_type":"{ [string]: number }"}],"returns":[{"desc":"whether the write applied","lua_type":"boolean?"},{"desc":"the `updates` table passed in","lua_type":"{ [string]: number }?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":393,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/CurrencyService.luau"}},{"name":"takeMultiple","desc":"Debits several balances in a single replicated mutation.\\n\\nEvery amount must be > 0, and \u2014 unless `override` is set \u2014 every balance is\\nchecked for affordability *before* any of them are debited, so the batch is\\nall-or-nothing: a player short on any one currency has none of them taken.\\n\\n:::caution Returns the deltas, not the balances\\nAs with [CurrencyService.addMultiple], the second return value is the\\n`updates` table you passed in, and the validation loop\'s `math.floor` is\\ndiscarded.\\n:::","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"balance owner","lua_type":"Player"},{"name":"updates","desc":"currencyType -> amount to debit","lua_type":"{ [string]: number }"},{"name":"override","desc":"allow balances to go negative","lua_type":"boolean?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"whether the debit applied","lua_type":"boolean?"},{"desc":"the `updates` table passed in","lua_type":"{ [string]: number }?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":441,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/CurrencyService.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"CurrencyService","desc":"The authoritative money path. Every currency balance in the game is read and\\nwritten through this service \u2014 nothing else should touch\\n`profile.stats.<currency>` directly.\\n\\nA currency type is any numeric key under `stats` in the profile\\n(`coins`, `gems`, `xp`, `points`, \u2026); the service is deliberately\\nstring-keyed rather than enumerated, so new currencies need no change here.\\n\\n## Write-through\\n\\nAll mutations funnel through one private `mutate` helper, which:\\n\\n1. Reads the live profile via [ProfileService.get] (bailing when unloaded).\\n2. Runs the caller\'s mutator against `profileData.stats` inside a pcall, so\\n   a throwing mutator warns and aborts instead of half-applying.\\n3. Derives the changed `stats.<currency>` paths from the mutator\'s returned\\n   table and hands them to [ProfileService.update], which pushes them to the\\n   player\'s replica and refreshes any matching leaderstat.\\n\\nBecause the mutator writes into the profile\'s own `stats` table, the profile\\nis updated in place; the [ProfileService.update] call is what makes the\\nchange visible to the client.\\n\\n## Guard rails\\n\\n[CurrencyService.set] rejects negative amounts; [CurrencyService.add] and\\n[CurrencyService.take] reject non-positive ones. `take` additionally refuses\\nto overdraw a balance unless the caller passes `override`, making it the\\nsafe default for spend flows. Singular `add`/`take` floor their amount, so\\nfractional currency can never enter the profile.\\n\\n## Regional pricing\\n\\n[CurrencyService.init] registers the `coins` developer-product callback with\\n[MarketplaceData]. Purchased coin grants are passed through\\n`adjustValueByUserPriceLevel` before crediting, so the amount awarded tracks\\nthe player\'s regional price level rather than the flat product value.\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":46,"path":"src/Server/Features/Core/CurrencyService.luau"}}')}}]);